-- title:
--   Function field of the base-changed two-chart model is generated by finite chart and base
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, $j \in F$ a nonzero element, and $S$ a commutative $R$-algebra. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin R F j`, the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements integral over $R[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {j}`, and let $\mathfrak X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and of the analogous algebra $A_{\infty}$ for $j^{-1}$ into the middle chart algebra, with structure morphism `toBase R F j : 𝔛 ⟶ Spec R` induced by the two structure maps. Put $\mathfrak X_S = \mathfrak X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} S$, the pullback of `toBase R F j` along `Spec.map` of $R \to S$, assume $\mathfrak X_S$ is an integral scheme, let $x$ be a point of $\mathfrak X_S$, and let $U \subseteq \mathfrak X_S$ be the preimage under the first projection of the open `(ιFin R F j) ''ᵁ ⊤`, the image of the finite chart, assumed nonempty. Then the function field of $\mathfrak X_S$ is generated as a subfield by the union of two subsets: the image of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ obtained by viewing $a \in A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ as a global section of $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, transporting it along the inverse of the isomorphism `(ιFin R F j).appIso ⊤` to a section of $\mathfrak X$ over the finite chart, pulling it back along the first projection to a section over $U$, and taking its germ in the function field; and the image of $S$ obtained by viewing $s \in S$ as a global section of $\operatorname{Spec} S$, pulling it back along the second projection to a global section of $\mathfrak X_S$, taking its germ at $x$, and mapping the stalk at $x$ into the function field. That is, the `Subfield.closure` of this union is $\top$.
--
--   This records that, after base change to an $R$-algebra $S$, the function field of the two-chart integral model attached to $(F,j)$ is generated by the finite chart algebra together with $S$; it is the generation statement underlying the identification of rational functions on the base-changed model. It is used in the analysis of the Deligne–Rapoport model package, in the two lemmas describing the behaviour of $\varphi$ and of the $j$-function on stalks at specialisations of points of the maximal ideal.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_subfieldClosure_range_germToFunctionField_union_range_eq_top.lean

